# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RingFlow — Environment Configuration Template
#
# Quick setup for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# RingFlow connects directly to PostgreSQL via Drizzle ORM and delivers real-time
# updates across all screens using Server-Sent Events (SSE) via /api/live.
# There is no external auth provider: sessions are cookies verified against Postgres.
#
# The server checks these at start-up (src/lib/env.ts) and refuses to start with
# a clear message if one is wrong. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. Database Connection (Required) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Direct PostgreSQL connection string used by Drizzle ORM, server actions, and scripts.
#
# • If running Docker Compose db on Windows/Linux localhost:
#   DATABASE_URL="postgres://event_suite:event_suite@127.0.0.1:5432/ringflow"
#
# • If running PostgreSQL inside a WSL2 container accessed from Windows host:
#   DATABASE_URL="postgres://event_suite:event_suite@<WSL_OR_CONTAINER_IP>:5432/ringflow"
#
# • For a hosted Postgres (RDS, Neon, Supabase Postgres, ...):
#   DATABASE_URL="postgres://<user>:<password>@<host>:5432/<db>"
DATABASE_URL="postgres://event_suite:event_suite@127.0.0.1:5432/ringflow"

# ── 2. Offline venue mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "true" on an air-gapped venue LAN: no calls to external services (Turnstile is skipped).
OFFLINE_MODE="false"

# ── 3. Bot Protection / Cloudflare Turnstile ──────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Set both to "disabled" (or leave OFFLINE_MODE="true") to turn Turnstile off.
# For an internet-facing deployment, create a widget at https://dash.cloudflare.com/ -> Turnstile.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY="disabled"
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY="disabled"

# ── 4. Public address (hosted / tunnel) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. The URL phones and spectators use to reach this server, e.g.
# "https://ringflow.example.org". Judge QR codes point here. Leave empty on a
# LAN-only install (QR codes then use the address the desk is browsing on).
# An event's own "tunnel URL" setting, when filled in, takes precedence for its judge QR codes.
APP_URL=""

# ── 5. Reverse proxy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "true" when a reverse proxy (nginx, Caddy, Cloudflare Tunnel) sits in front and
# appends the real client address to X-Forwarded-For. Rate limits then key on
# that address. Leave "false" when browsers talk to Node directly.
TRUST_PROXY="false"

# ── 6. Embedding the scoreboard ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Who may show /scoreboard and /public pages inside a frame (OBS,
# a venue display system). CSP frame-ancestors syntax. Default: same origin only.
# FRAME_ANCESTORS="'self' https://obs.example.org"
FRAME_ANCESTORS=""
